  "Question": "In a group of cows and chickens, the number of legs was \\(14\\) more than twice the number of heads. The number of cows was:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(5\\)",
    "B": "\\(7\\)",
    "C": "\\(10\\)",
    "D": "\\(12\\)",
    "E": "\\(14\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "Imagine first that every animal is a chicken. Since each animal has one head, this would give exactly twice as many legs as heads.\n\nReplacing an imagined chicken with a cow leaves the head count unchanged but adds \\(4-2=2\\) legs. All \\(14\\) extra legs must come from cows, so the number of cows is\n\\[\n14\\div2=7.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(7\\), choice B.",
